Eligibility note: L40 and A6000 have been dropped — the 6000 Ada (960 GB/s, NVLink-pairable, workstation-grade) replaces them as the 48GB intelligence pick; the L40S is the FP8-speed alternative; the RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (96GB, NVFP4) is the step to the frontier class. Weigh the 6000 Ada's ~0.70 $/hr against the L40S's lower power draw if $/token at high volume matters more than peak capacity.

Bottom line — "we're hunting intelligence"
Intelligence scales with VRAM, not the card name. 3090 = 4090 in capability; the 5090 adds ~one step (fidelity + speed); the RTX 6000 Ada is the true IQ jump — the only card here that fits an 80B-MoE/70B-dense brain.
Max local intelligence per dollar → RTX 6000 Ada running Qwen3-Coder-Next 80B (max IQ + MoE speed), with 70B-dense and dual-MoE as alternates. NVLink adds a future 96GB path.
If speed + full-context + modern stack matter more than ceiling → 5090, but only with vLLM/TensorRT so the NVFP4 path is real; on Ollama it's just a fast 32GB card.
4090 over 3090 is almost never an intelligence upgrade. Spend the difference on capacity instead.
Be honest about the frontier. GLM-5.2 / DeepSeek V4 are API-only at 10–30× your size and lead on hard reasoning + 1M context. At 0.70 $/hr even the 6000 Ada can cost more per token than DeepSeek V4-Flash — local is a privacy / sovereignty / unlimited-volume play now, and the only way to hold a frontier-adjacent brain entirely in your own hands.
Model selection dominates hardware. Qwen3-Coder-Next 80B or Qwen3.8-27B (reasoning), Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B (agentic coding), DeepSeek-R1:32b (hard math). The card only decides how high a quant / how long a context you can afford it at — and on the 48GB card, whether you finally reach the 80B class.
Assumptions & caveats: t/s are memory-bandwidth-scaled estimates from 3090-measured bases (6000 Ada ≈ 3090-class decode for same-size models). The 5090 NVFP4 column assumes vLLM/TensorRT-LLM; the GGUF column is the Ollama path. 6000 Ada run cost pegged at 0.70 $/hr (user-specified). Frontier API prices are list rates as of mid-2026; DeepSeek V4 uses off-peak/peak time-of-day billing. $/1M figures use each card's blended hourly window — verify fit/speed with ollama ps (100% GPU) or your engine's metrics on the actual card.
